<title>FRANCE: Bonus issue boosts Cetelem, Bancaire.</title>
<headline>Bonus issue boosts Cetelem, Bancaire.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in consumer finance and leasing house Compagnie Bancaire and its Cetelem subsidiary rose on Thursday, boosted by news of Cetelem's bonus share issue, market sources said.</p>
<p>Cetelem rose 2.18 percent to 1,264 francs, after peaking at 1,280, on volume of 45,805 shares at 1437 GMT. Bancaire was up 2.63 percent at 585 francs on 93,109 shares. One source said a big brokerage was due to issue a very favourable note.</p>
<p>Cetelem said on Wednesday it would issue one free share for every one share held and pay a 10 franc dividend on the enlarged capital, effectively doubling the payout.  </p>
<p>&quot;This decision shows a certain confidence in the future,&quot; said a fund manager.</p>
<p>Bancaire owns 63 percent of Cetelem.</p>
